    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0794" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1949: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-03T19:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">January 3,
                                1921—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 4—12:22
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>2. Personal attention Norman Davis<anchor n="2" xml:id="d640-f1"/> and Third
                    Assistant Secretary of State:<anchor n="3" xml:id="d640-f2"/></p>
                <p>After sending January 3, 5 p.m. President Menocal invited me to Palace and in the
                    presence of Minister for Foreign Affairs explained <pb facs="0795" n="671"
                        xml:id="pg671"/> that he could not receive General Crowder because of the
                    manner in which he has been [sent]. President Menocal appeared deeply aggrieved
                    and asserted that he had endeavored to work in harmony with our Government and
                    he could not understand General Crowder’s being sent on a warship without our
                    first observing the formalities customary among friendly nations. After a
                    prolonged discussion Menocal stated that should Crowder’s arrival be delayed
                    until there could be an exchange of notes stating the fundamental reasons for
                    his visit, that he would be disposed to give favorable consideration to having
                    the General continue his journey. The notes are evidently to be used as basis
                    for communication to press and I urgently request instruction as to the
                    Department’s attitude and what steps if any are to be taken by the Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
